\f0\fs28\b How to Set CORS Origin in Django\b0\fs22\par
\fs20\b Tandermis \emdash  Backend CORS Configuration Guide\b0\fs22\par
\par
This guide explains how to allow your Next.js frontend to call your Django API without browser CORS errors.\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 1: Install django-cors-headers\b0\fs22\par
\par
Run in your Django project environment:\par
\par
\f1 pip install django-cors-headers\f0\par
\par
Add to requirements.txt:\par
\f1 django-cors-headers>=4.0.0\f0\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 2: Add to INSTALLED_APPS\b0\fs22\par
\par
Open settings.py and add:\par
\par
\f1 INSTALLED_APPS = [\par
    ...\par
    "corsheaders",\par
    ...\par
]\f0\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 3: Add the Middleware (order matters)\b0\fs22\par
\par
Add CorsMiddleware as high as possible, right after SecurityMiddleware:\par
\par
\f1 MIDDLEWARE = [\par
    "django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware",\par
    "corsheaders.middleware.CorsMiddleware",\par
    "django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware",\par
    ...\par
]\f0\par
\par
\b Important:\b0  If CorsMiddleware is placed too low, CORS headers may not be applied correctly.\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 4: Set Allowed Origins\b0\fs22\par
\par
\f1 CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS = [\par
    "http://localhost:3000",\par
    "http://127.0.0.1:3000",\par
    "https://tandermis.com",\par
    "https://www.tandermis.com",\par
]\f0\par
\par
\b Rules:\b0\par
\bullet  Use the exact origin (scheme + host + port).\par
\bullet  No trailing slash.\par
\bullet  Do not use wildcards.\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 5 (Optional): Allow Credentials\b0\fs22\par
\par
\f1 CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS = True\f0\par
\par
Only needed for cookies/session auth. Not required for Bearer JWT tokens.\par
\par

\fs24\b Step 6: Restart Django\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b Local:\b0  python manage.py runserver\par
\b PythonAnywhere:\b0  Reload the web app from the dashboard\par
\par

\fs24\b Recommended Setup for Tandermis\b0\fs22\par
\par
\f1 CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS = [\par
    "http://localhost:3000",\par
    "http://127.0.0.1:3000",\par
    "https://tandermis.com",\par
    "https://www.tandermis.com",\par
]\f0\par
\par

\fs24\b What NOT to Do in Production\b0\fs22\par
\par
\cf3 CORS_ALLOW_ALL_ORIGINS = True\cf0  \emdash  Avoid in production. Allows any website to call your API.\par
\par

\fs24\b Troubleshooting\b0\fs22\par
\par
1. Check the browser error \emdash  origin must match CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS exactly.\par
2. Verify middleware order.\par
3. Reload PythonAnywhere after settings changes.\par
4. Ensure no proxy strips CORS headers.\par
\par
\b Example error:\b0\par
\f1 Access blocked by CORS policy from origin 'http://localhost:3000'\f0\par
\b Fix:\b0  Add "http://localhost:3000" to CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.\par
\par

\fs24\b Quick Checklist\b0\fs22\par
\par
\bullet  pip install django-cors-headers\par
\bullet  Add "corsheaders" to INSTALLED_APPS\par
\bullet  Add CorsMiddleware near top of MIDDLEWARE\par
\bullet  Set CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS\par
\bullet  Restart Django / reload PythonAnywhere\par
\bullet  Test login or signup from frontend\par
\par

